  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acute Watery Diarrhea (AWD)/Cholera Outbreak Response Plan-2022 (Oxfam in Syria)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in Syria has the following three strategies to respond to the Cholera outbreak: Installation of 5 water tanks in Seglaiah (Jabal Saman sub  -district) that were provided by SARC on request of Local water establishment and WASH sub  -sector Cleaning the ground water tank in Jebrin (Jabal Saman sub  -district) on request of Local water establishment and WASH sub  -sector Cleaning 4 of 8 ground water tanks (prioritized and in the process) in Aleppo city on the request of Local water establishment and WASH sub  -sector&#xa0; A community awareness campaign about diarrheal diseases/Cholera and water treatment is taking place in Eastern rural Aleppo, in Handarat (Aleppo city), and in Sheikh Maksoud under other projects. Oxfam will conduct mass media health education campaigns focused on hygiene practices (handwashing, sanitation, water storage, food handling) in communities and education facilities. The IEC material will be the one that is agreed by MoH, WHO, and the sector to share one message. Oxfam will use a multi  -channel approach to promote the campaign including billboards, banners, sessions, social media, etc. Oxfam will capacitate the already formed community  -based volunteers to promote AWD/Cholera  -related sessions to their local community along with supporting/guiding them in preparing Salt Sugar Solutions (SSS)/ORS and its use along with referral to health centers/CTC in case of AWD/Cholera. Oxfam will also conduct orientation and awareness sessions for staff, partners, CBVs, community, schools, and health centers. Oxfam will identify key risk spots in markets e.g., ice factories/sellers, and restaurants to share IEC and do sessions on safe water chain management and good hygiene practices. Oxfam will also monitor practices.</narrative>
  </description>
